---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="about — ollie"
  description="ollie is built by people with adhd, for people with adhd. private by design, opt-in research, no analytics."
>
  <article class="prose about">
    <p class="meta">about</p>

    <h1>made by people who needed it.</h1>

    <p>
      ollie started because the existing tools did not fit. calendar apps assume
      you remember to open them. habit trackers assume you forgot once. budget
      apps assume the problem is math. journals assume you have the energy to
      type a paragraph at the end of a day that already broke you.
    </p>

    <p>
      adhd is not a productivity bug. it is a different operating system. ollie
      is the tool you would have built for yourself if you had the time, which
      you do not, because you have adhd.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>private by design</h2>

    <p>
      your data lives on your device. it is encrypted with a passphrase only
      you know. if you sync across devices, the encryption happens before the
      data leaves your device. ollie's server sees ciphertext for your module
      content, and your email in plaintext so you can sign in.
    </p>

    <p>
      ollie does not run advertising. ollie does not sell data. ollie does not
      load analytics scripts on this site or in the app outside of the
      bare-minimum crash diagnostics required to ship fixes.
    </p>

    <h2>opt-in research</h2>

    <p>
      ollie is building an adhd research corpus. the corpus is built from
      anonymized, pii-scrubbed text contributions — and only if you opt in.
      the default is off. opting in is reversible going forward; past
      contributions, having no identifier linking them to you, stay in the
      corpus.
    </p>

    <p>
      this is the trade ollie offers in plain sentences: contribute to the
      research that benefits the next adhd brain who installs the app, or do
      not. neither answer changes what the app does for you.
    </p>

    <h2>what ollie is not</h2>

    <p>
      ollie is not a medical device. ollie is not a psychiatrist. ollie is not
      a financial advisor. ollie is not a crisis service. ollie is a tool for
      tracking your own life, with patterns surfaced where they help, and
      friction removed where the existing tools added it.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>where ollie is going</h2>

    <p>
      ollie is in private beta. the iphone build is the first home. desktop
      follows. the modules — finance, cycle, body, habits, goals, work,
      grocery, pets, journal, admin, brain dump — ship one at a time, polished
      before they leave the lab.
    </p>

    <p>
      if you want in: <a href="mailto:support@ollie.app?subject=waitlist">support@ollie.app</a>.
      one line, your device, what part of life is breaking. we read every one.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
</style>
